#define EUDAIMON_OBSERVER_ENTRY 0
static const u8 sEudaimonObserver_1[] = _("The light shines upon those who walk with purpose, and upon those who have lost theirs, and does not ask which you are. Open this book when it is barely light. It was not written for the world you walk at night.\pA LARK read it under a tree that sings, an hour and a half before the sun, when the day is still being made. She says she did not go anywhere. She says she stayed, and it came.\pThe other two books are careful. This one is gentle, which is not the same. The words in green are not for saying loudly: breathe them.\pThere is another way to read this. It was read in the dark, by someone braver than he looks. Do not be afraid of it.\pIs any of it true?\pHold it lightly. Then ask what it would give you, if it were.\pYour daemon looks up at you, bright as the morning.");
static const u8 sEudaimonObserver_2[] = _("The light shines upon those who walk with purpose, and upon those who have lost theirs, and does not ask which you are. Open this book when it is barely light. It was not written for the world you walk at night.\pA LARK read it under a tree that sings, an hour and a half before the sun, when the day is still being made. She says she did not go anywhere. She says she stayed, and it came.\pThe other two books are careful. This one is gentle, which is not the same. The words in green are not for saying loudly: breathe them.\pThere is another way to read this. It was read in the dark, by someone braver than he looks. Do not be afraid of it.\pIs any of it true?\pHold it lightly. Then ask what it would give you, if it were.\pYour daemon does not look up yet. It will.");
